      "path": "/books/al-kafi:4:3:21:23",
      "text": [
        " سَأَلْتُ أَبَا عَبْدِ اللَّهِ ( عليه السلام ) عَنْ بَيْضَةِ نَعَامَةٍ أَكَلْتُ فِي الْحَرَمِ قَالَ تَصَدَّقْ بِثَمَنِهَا ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ahmad, from Al Hassan, from Ali Bin Al Numan, from Sa’d Bin Abdullah who said, ",
          "‘I asked Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> about an ostrich egg which I ate in the Al-Harram. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Give in charity with its price’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "23. Ahmad ibn al-Hassan has narrated from Ali ibn al-Nu’man from Sa‘d ibn ‘Abd Allah who has said the following: “I once asked abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, about the case of my eating ostrich eggs in al-Haram (the sacred area). He (the Imam) said, ‘You must give its price in charity.’” "
        ]
      }
